# Devops/operations properties override file for bff.
#
# This is the explicit, per-service override file configured via the 'application-properties-config' Tomcat
# context environment entry (see conf/ocp/bff.xml) / Jetty EnvEntry (see src/test/jetty/jetty-env.xml), and
# loaded by ServiceConfig.initialize(configFile, propertiesOverrideFile). It is meant for devops/operations
# secrets and per-environment values that must never be committed to git.
#
# Copy this file to 'bff-application.properties' (same folder, without the '.SAMPLE' suffix) and fill in your
# own values. This filename is already covered by the repository's generic '*-application.properties'
# .gitignore rule.
#
# Any key present in bff-base.yaml can be overridden here, using the same dotted path. Like every other setting,
# this file is picked up by the auto-reload thread too (see config.autoupdate in bff-base.yaml): editing and
# saving it takes effect within config.autoupdate.intervalms milliseconds, without a service restart.

# keycloak.secret=changeme
# secretSalt=changeme

# apis.ds-image.baseURL=https://localhost/
# apis.poc-middleware.baseURL=http://localhost:9061
